Package: immunread
Title: Convenient Parsers for Popular Immune Repertoire Data Formats
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Vadim I.", "Nazarov", , "support@immunomind.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3659-2709"))
Contact: support@immunomind.com
Description: Provides ready-to-use parser functions for importing adaptive
    immune receptor repertoire (AIRR) tables into 'ImmunData'
    objects. It focuses on the AIRR Community format as the canonical format
    and also includes parsers for common tool-specific outputs: 'MiXCR',
    '10xGenomics', 'BD Genomics', 'Adaptive Biotechnologies', 'Dandelion',
    'Immcantation', 'ParseBio', 'Trust4', 'WAT3R'.
License: Apache License (>= 2)
URL: https://immunomind.github.io/docs/, https://github.com/immunomind/immunread
BugReports: https://github.com/immunomind/immunread/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0),
    immundata (>= 0.1.0)
Imports:
    dplyr,
    duckplyr (>= 1.2.1),
    rlang
Suggests: 
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    readr
